{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/1126479-sidereal-exalted-and-arcane-fate","id":1126479,"title":"Sidereal Exalted and Arcane Fate","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Sidereal Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-08-08T15:37:40-07:00","id":1126479,"title":"Sidereal Exalted and Arcane Fate","content":"In all my years of being Exalted fan, there is one subject that hasn't been addressed that darn well needs to be:<br /> <br /> Arcane Fate is fucking terrifying.<br /> <br /> Just consider for a moment, the idea of the world forgetting you exist. As far as everyone outside of Yu-Shan is concerned, you were never born.<br /> <br /> &quot;But Jimborg,&quot; you say, &quot;the rules for Arcane Fate say that even if someone conclusively forgets you exist, you can remind them.&quot;<br /> <br /> And that's true, you can do that. But I want you to consider, how fucked up it is, for example, for a parent struggle to remember their child. Your best friend whom you've know you entire life doesn't know who you are. To have someone show up out of the blue and <i>insist </i>they are your significant other, whom you have loved for years, and you <i>swear</i> you have never seen them before in your life.<br /> <br /> And this doesn't even touch on other, more insidious aspects of Arcane Fate: every record that can be directly attributed to you, personally, is eventually stolen away by the Loom of Fate. And unlike the memories of others, there is no recovery clause. This is no way to get them back. No way to recover that childhood toy. No way to find the deed for your house. And you can just forget about finding your lunch in the company fridge.<br /> <br /> And this is <i>never </i>addressed in-universe. Not in MoEP: Sidreals, and not in CoCD: Yu-Shan. As far as the canon Sidereals are concerned, the psychological elements of Arcane Fate simply don't exist. And I think that's a shame, because this is a story telling hook that is <i>really </i>underutilized.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>What do we want? 3rd Edition Sidereals!<br /> When do we want it? In accordance with the dictates of Fate!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/867-jimborg","name":"Jimborg","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-08T17:20:11-07:00","id":1126509,"title":"","content":"I agree. If a mechanic like that is going to be included, it should be used for some dramatic purpose. Personally, I've never much enjoyed Arcane Fate, as it seems aggravating to deal with unless Sidereal PCs ONLY work with other Sids or within Yu-Shan.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>She/Her pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12975-zealot_vedas","name":"Zealot_Vedas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12975_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-08T17:31:55-07:00","id":1126512,"title":"","content":"Arcane Fate only works if you're gone for more than a few days, and its effect can be lessened with a prolonged relationship.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-09T00:01:27-07:00","id":1126604,"title":"","content":"I think it might also be why the sids need to put so much effort into tracking down and training their pre-exalts early, get them enmeshed with other sids and Yu-Shan so when that happens everything they care about is already immune to the effect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11837-a-not-quite-simple-soul","name":"A Not Quite Simple Soul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-09T00:51:05-07:00","id":1126615,"title":"","content":"Other Sidereals and Gods in the Bureau of Destiny are immune to Arcane Fate. Your parents will forget you ever existed, but you're also going to be away training to become a Vizier for upwards of 20 years. As far as the Bureau is concerned there is no drawback. Everyone you need to have remember you will; your connections to Creation are severed so the entire &quot;I disappear for years while my friends and family age and die&quot; thing is lessened. Sidereals are always fated to have become a Sidereal. A Journeys will be born with wanderlust; you have a new adventure, no need to concern yourself with the old. Endings are born fatalistic; this is how it will end, as it was foretold as it is known. <br /> By time you become a fully fledged member of the Bureau of Destiny, you've probably learned to cope or burned out. I think however the inability to cope with Arcane fate is a great way for Rakan Thulio to draw in unsuspecting, impressionable, young Sidereals and turn them against heaven","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1089921-new-sidereal-homebrew-for-3e-down-came-the-spider\" target=\"_blank\">Down Came the Spider</a>, my 3e Sidereal Conversion! Please comment<br /> Homebrewer of many things","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11713-zx_xz","name":"ZX_XZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11713_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-09T01:22:15-07:00","id":1126617,"title":"","content":"I have certainly made use of it for my sid characters. Arcane Fate is horrible and alienating and a massive punch to the gut for a newly awakened Sidereal, and going &quot;AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAA&quot; while doing the Kermit arms is an <i>entirely reasonable</i> reaction. Unlike the other Celestial Exalt types, becoming a Sid <i>kind of sucks</i>.<br /> <br /> (And then you get pressured into a literal job for life, as in you are not getting out of the job while alive, where you're told you skipping on the job could have dire consequences for the state of reality, so generally speaking either you learn to cope or become bitter and jaded as all fuck).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1793,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1793-drascin","user":"Drascin","date":". 08-09-2017, 04:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1793-drascin","name":"Drascin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1793_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"400"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-09T08:26:09-07:00","id":1126723,"title":"","content":"This is <i>brutal</i>. And they brought Arcane Fate upon themselves? I seem to remember they worked a ritual after the Usurpation to make Creation forget their existence, and this is the result.<br /> <br /> Also, shit, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1793-drascin\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1793_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1793\" data-vbnamecard=\"1793\">Drascin</a>, you made your case. That must be one of the most god-awful Exaltations around - chaining you to a desk for centuries? Fuck, I'll never play a Sid. Unless I develop some masochistic fetish, that is.<br /> <br /> <i>Sidereals: Exaltation that tastes like despair</i>.<br /> <br /> (Although the devs said in this edition they'll be more like 007... let's hope so O_o )","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13651-roswynn","name":"Roswynn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13651_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"173"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-09T09:09:43-07:00","id":1126736,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Roswynn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/1126479-sidereal-exalted-and-arcane-fate?p=1126723#post1126723\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is <i>brutal</i>. And they brought Arcane Fate upon themselves? I seem to remember they worked a ritual after the Usurpation to make Creation forget their existence, and this is the result.</div> </div> </div> </div>Arcane Fate, at least last edition, was kind of an accident. They were trying to hide the Usurpation in order to not end up all dead, and they discovered that constellations <i>do</i> have a maximum stress point the empirical way, ie it basically exploded on them from overload. Someone really should have written down the system specifications and maximum load somewhere, but mythological creators are not, on the whole, super big on proper system documentation :P<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Roswynn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/1126479-sidereal-exalted-and-arcane-fate?p=1126723#post1126723\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, shit, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1793-drascin\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1793_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1793\" data-vbnamecard=\"1793\">Drascin</a>, you made your case. That must be one of the most god-awful Exaltations around - chaining you to a desk for centuries? Fuck, I'll never play a Sid. Unless I develop some masochistic fetish, that is.<br /> <br /> <i>Sidereals: Exaltation that tastes like despair</i>.<br /> <br /> (Although the devs said in this edition they'll be more like 007... let's hope so O_o )</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bIt's not really that it's a desk job. Like, it's an organization, desk job is going to be there, but it's almost certainly a lot more running everywhere desperately putting out fires and saving the world with two pieces of gum, a slingshot, and a water gun watch Q gave you, than writing at a desk.<br /> <br /> It's more that it's kind of a hideously important job that only you can do by <i>definition</i>, into which you get drafted right after you get the gut punch of getting forcibly removed from your previous life. It seems like the kind of thing that could breed some frustration - you have a job you're probably going to get killed in at some point, cause there's a <i>reason</i> Kejak is an extreme rarity in dying from old age, you got uprooted in a fairly distressing way when you got the abilities that let you do it in the first place, and you can't even quit if you have a conscience cause there's like eighty of you guys for the entire world and every single hand is necessary.<br /> <br /> Like, there's a reason I think @Coik used to meme that being a Sidereal might equally mean that the Maidens liked you or that they hated your guts, cause the end result is kind of indstinguishable :P.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1793,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1793-drascin","user":"Drascin","date":". 08-09-2017, 12:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1793-drascin","name":"Drascin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1793_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"400"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-10T14:26:07-07:00","id":1127328,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Drascin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/1126479-sidereal-exalted-and-arcane-fate?p=1126736#post1126736\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Arcane Fate, at least last edition, was kind of an accident. They were trying to hide the Usurpation in order to not end up all dead, and they discovered that constellations <i>do</i> have a maximum stress point the empirical way, ie it basically exploded on them from overload. Someone really should have written down the system specifications and maximum load somewhere, but mythological creators are not, on the whole, super big on proper system documentation :P</div> </div> </div> </div>Also, they could have run a couple tests to see if what they wanted to achieve was actually gonna backfire and erase them from everyone's memory. Or they could've asked a pattern spider, idk...<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Drascin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/1126479-sidereal-exalted-and-arcane-fate?p=1126736#post1126736\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not really that it's a desk job. Like, it's an organization, desk job is going to be there, but it's almost certainly a lot more running everywhere desperately putting out fires and saving the world with two pieces of gum, a slingshot, and a water gun watch Q gave you, than writing at a desk.<br /> <br /> It's more that it's kind of a hideously important job that only you can do by <i>definition</i>, into which you get drafted right after you get the gut punch of getting forcibly removed from your previous life. It seems like the kind of thing that could breed some frustration - you have a job you're probably going to get killed in at some point, cause there's a <i>reason</i> Kejak is an extreme rarity in dying from old age, you got uprooted in a fairly distressing way when you got the abilities that let you do it in the first place, and you can't even quit if you have a conscience cause there's like eighty of you guys for the entire world and every single hand is necessary.<br /> <br /> Like, there's a reason I think @Coik used to meme that being a Sidereal might equally mean that the Maidens liked you or that they hated your guts, cause the end result is kind of indstinguishable :P.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh well, that's a bit better. I mean, yeah, working all the time to avoid Creation implodes and dying on the job without a shred of thanks from the mortals you saved are not really high on my list of priorities, but at least there's gonna be some adventure that way. But can't they never rest? Do something just for fun? A little R&amp;R? I get they're Exalted, but they're gonna suffer from severe burnout if they're never cut some slack. I imagine most Sids would turn to drugs. Maybe the Beasts of Resplendent Liquids were created with them in mind ;P<br /> <br /> Sure, being taken from your life like that sounds quite traumatic, too. Maybe Ketchup turned out the way he did b/c of all the compound stress? And he's still relatively well-adjusted, I mean, he just plotted the wholesale slaughter of a few hundreds Celestials after all...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13651-roswynn","name":"Roswynn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13651_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"173"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-10T15:31:15-07:00","id":1127367,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Roswynn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/1126479-sidereal-exalted-and-arcane-fate?p=1127328#post1127328\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200b[COLOR=#252C2F][FONT=Helvetica][SIZE=13px]<br /> Oh well, that's a bit better. I mean, yeah, working all the time to avoid Creation implodes and dying on the job without a shred of thanks from the mortals you saved are not really high on my list of priorities, but at least there's gonna be some adventure that way. But can't they never rest? Do something just for fun? A little R&amp;R? I get they're Exalted, but they're gonna suffer from severe burnout if they're never cut some slack. I imagine most Sids would turn to drugs. Maybe the Beasts of Resplendent Liquids were created with them in mind ;P<br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, its certainly not constant running around. You are allowed to have several weeks sabbatical per year depending on your Salary rating. A large portion of the drudgery can be passed off on to Secretarial gods. It's a common mistake I see among STs who aren't that into Sidereals is following the meme of &quot;Constant work, no sleep, Creation is constantly falling apart at the seams&quot;. A huge amount of Sidereal work is showing up at the right place at the right time, saying something and leaving because they know what will happen if they change something small. Playing as a Sidereal should be fun, you should be able to relish in the fact that you are a mighty being who knows all, see's all and can plan all, shaping Creation for the better (and to your personal goals) from the shadows.<br /> IMO one of the best ways to play Sidereals is a bit like playing Shadowrun. You get a mission of a goal that must be accomplished, and then are dispatched into Creation to fulfill said goal without accidentally breaking the masquerade. Along the way you'll have problems because of personal goals conflicting with the mission, jobs from your Convention or Faction that are counterproductive to said mission and missions that are counterproductive to yourselves. And its you and your circle's jobs to navigate this tangled web to make the world a better place. Then you have sessions set in Yu-Shan which will be more conflict with the system and other Sidereals, where your goals will clash with others as you try to lobby for your Convention at a planning committee, expose the corruption of your superior, or deal with the dangerous crime rings that lurk in the slums of the Heavenly city.<br /> Also a note, if you have friends that you cannot bear have forget you, there are several charms that let them remember you in several trees. Of course most of them have side effects or limited numbers of uses but its always an option. You are a Sidereal, fate bends at your whim; the last thing you are is helpless in the face of your goals","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1089921-new-sidereal-homebrew-for-3e-down-came-the-spider\" target=\"_blank\">Down Came the Spider</a>, my 3e Sidereal Conversion! Please comment<br /> Homebrewer of many things","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11713-zx_xz","name":"ZX_XZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11713_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-10T15:44:53-07:00","id":1127379,"title":"","content":"The Sidereal dictionary defines &quot;vacation&quot; as that time between the death of one of your Exaltation's hosts and your next incarnation. (That's the part that REALLY sucks - Sidereal Exaltations carry past life memories much more reliably than other types, meaning from a certain perspective, it isn't just a &quot;for life&quot; job, but a job you've had for eons and will continue to have until the end of everything.) Although depending on your sources, the &quot;training period&quot; for Sidereals is actually relatively pleasant. It still involves hard training, but with a lot less of the pressure, and Heaven is surprisingly forward on the whole &quot;let kids have childhoods&quot; front. Not to mention that as far as standard of living goes, Heaven is WAY more pleasant than anywhere in Creation, so even if you're working long, grueling hours, you'll have a very nice place to go home at the end of the day/mission.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12682-remedy","name":"Remedy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12682_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"90"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-10T16:54:04-07:00","id":1127401,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Remedy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/1126479-sidereal-exalted-and-arcane-fate?p=1127379#post1127379\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Sidereal dictionary defines &quot;vacation&quot; as that time between the death of one of your Exaltation's hosts and your next incarnation.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is an untrue stereotype that has been bouncing around this forum for the longest time and it causes a lot of people to really worry about playing Sidereals. Lets look at what the books actually say about vacation times<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MOEP: Sidereals, Page 53</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">SABBATICAL<br /> <br /> The Bureau of Destiny does not insist that Sidereals spend every waking moment on Bureau business. Every now and then, Viziers can take vacations, which the Bureau calls sabbaticals. While on sabbatical, a Vizier can pursue her own interests.<br /> <br /> Some Sidereals use their sabbaticals to unwind\u2014which could mean anything from lolling on a beach in Wavecrest to competing in one of Creation\u2019s martial arts tournaments. These Sidereals often use their sabbaticals to reconnect with humanity: they can spend some time being an ordinary person, doing ordinary things. (Of course, they need to use a resplendent destiny if they want to interact with other people very much.) After years spent among protocol-crazy gods or facing danger on the Maidens\u2019 secret service, just spending an evening at a caravanserai, drinking and swap-ping bawdy songs with the drovers and merchants, can seem sweeter than Heaven\u2019s finest Ambrosia.</div> </div> </div> </div>Little later down it says you can take up to one month per year vacation time, with higher backing allowing you to take more. That's a not insignificant amount of time off, although less valuable than a month IRL as Creation has longer years.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1089921-new-sidereal-homebrew-for-3e-down-came-the-spider\" target=\"_blank\">Down Came the Spider</a>, my 3e Sidereal Conversion! Please comment<br /> Homebrewer of many things","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11713-zx_xz","name":"ZX_XZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11713_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-10T17:39:40-07:00","id":1127412,"title":"","content":"Arcane Fate is a big reason why the Sidereal spend so much time in Yu-Shan, since they can actually have relationships with the gods and spirits there, and also why they tend to have a rather divorced feeling from humanity as a whole. Unlike the other Exalted, the Sidereal can't really live among humans for long (without creating disguises and pretending to be someone they're not). Thus they are people who spend their lives protecting humans, and yet who can never truly exist among humanity and this psychological impact probably helps to somewhat explain the attitude many elder Sidereal have, viewing humanity as merely numbers and statistics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-11T05:01:42-07:00","id":1127567,"title":"","content":"There's a lot of aspects of Sidereals that have been pushed way beyond the point of parody through a mixture of fanon and people picking up where better writers left off. Arcane Fate (or at least its presentation) is probably some component of this that I hope gets scrutinised for 3rd edition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-11T06:18:31-07:00","id":1127589,"title":"","content":"Heyy, who else remembers the Acquaintances Background?<br /> <br /> And the Charm that allowed you to automatically dole out the Acquaintances Background?<br /> <br /> \u200bWell, it's a nuance deviating from an easily parsed and kind of &quot;funny&quot; reduction, so probably nobody.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-11T13:44:18-07:00","id":1127770,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZX_XZ</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/1126479-sidereal-exalted-and-arcane-fate?p=1127367#post1127367\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, its certainly not constant running around. You are allowed to have several weeks sabbatical per year depending on your Salary rating. A large portion of the drudgery can be passed off on to Secretarial gods. It's a common mistake I see among STs who aren't that into Sidereals is following the meme of &quot;Constant work, no sleep, Creation is constantly falling apart at the seams&quot;. A huge amount of Sidereal work is showing up at the right place at the right time, saying something and leaving because they know what will happen if they change something small. Playing as a Sidereal should be fun, you should be able to relish in the fact that you are a mighty being who knows all, see's all and can plan all, shaping Creation for the better (and to your personal goals) from the shadows.<br /> IMO one of the best ways to play Sidereals is a bit like playing Shadowrun. You get a mission of a goal that must be accomplished, and then are dispatched into Creation to fulfill said goal without accidentally breaking the masquerade. Along the way you'll have problems because of personal goals conflicting with the mission, jobs from your Convention or Faction that are counterproductive to said mission and missions that are counterproductive to yourselves. And its you and your circle's jobs to navigate this tangled web to make the world a better place. Then you have sessions set in Yu-Shan which will be more conflict with the system and other Sidereals, where your goals will clash with others as you try to lobby for your Convention at a planning committee, expose the corruption of your superior, or deal with the dangerous crime rings that lurk in the slums of the Heavenly city.<br /> Also a note, if you have friends that you cannot bear have forget you, there are several charms that let them remember you in several trees. Of course most of them have side effects or limited numbers of uses but its always an option. You are a Sidereal, fate bends at your whim; the last thing you are is helpless in the face of your goals</div> </div> </div> </div>Now I'm starting to like them. Vacations, yay! Passing off crap jobs to your underlings! Lobbying and politicking! Charms that let people remember you!<br /> <br /> I really dig your description. I hope Sids keep being this awesome in this edition (actually I'm fairly trustful of the devs, so I see no reason why they shouldn't. The War in Heaven narrative should even enhance the whole thing, IMVHO).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13651-roswynn","name":"Roswynn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13651_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"173"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-11T14:11:57-07:00","id":1127778,"title":"","content":"I'd note, even considering sabbaticals, if you've got a Sidereal who is ultimately spending the majority of their time in Yu-Shan, the difference between Arcane Fate and being mundanely forgotten is mostly a matter of a bit of mystical veneer that reinforces the character of Sidereal Exalted.<br /> <br /> \u200bThat comic in Manual: Sidereals? Where a bunch of washer women struggle to remember details about some hero who saved them a few years back? That's the kind of thing that would happen no matter what they were (assuming that nobody made a practice of repeating a description of them once a week or accurately painted them or something). Much the same for that shopkeeper who struggles to remember May Blossom; I would say that it's not uncommon for people who have casual sex encounters to have a hard time remembering the details a year or so later (something that I say with no stigma or judgment whatsoever).<br /> <br /> \u200bOr with parents; assuming that the Sidereal is somebody who, having been given access to the whole of the world still wishes to periodically visit their parents (while likely drawing from cultural inputs that don't really have things like telecommunications to condition the idea that maintaining a lifelong relationship with them when you don't live within walking distance is the norm), there are means and a bit of magic to allow that, and even then it's only a concern for a very small part of the Exalt's life. In most cases though, I would say that it's not too much different from, say, being an early European colonist to the Americas (or from one end of America to the other, during western expansion) of modest means, in which the departure means that neither shall see or communicate with one another for the rest of their lives. The difference of actually forgetting that you existed might be a bit distressing, but if you were never going to see them again anyway, the practical difference to your life is kind of minimal.<br /> <br /> \u200bThe main thing about Arcane Fate is not what it does to the individual (as viewed through a lens of modern circumstances and relationships), but what it's done to widespread awareness of the Sidereal Exalted. If a Dynast saves a village, odds are that the villagers will forget everything about them except that they were a Dynast in a few years, and some generations after even that detail (and that any saving was done) might be lost, and if you introduce yourself as a Dynast or Dragon Blooded many people are likely to get what you are. Sidereals just get an additional effect that means that they happen to not get even that (and by the institutions through which the Sidereal Exalted exert control over the world, that's kind of how they like it anyway).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-12T02:05:43-07:00","id":1127980,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Roswynn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/1126479-sidereal-exalted-and-arcane-fate?p=1127328#post1127328\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh well, that's a bit better. I mean, yeah, working all the time to avoid Creation implodes and dying on the job without a shred of thanks from the mortals you saved are not really high on my list of priorities, but at least there's gonna be some adventure that way. But can't they never rest? Do something just for fun? A little R&amp;R? I get they're Exalted, but they're gonna suffer from severe burnout if they're never cut some slack. I imagine most Sids would turn to drugs. Maybe the Beasts of Resplendent Liquids were created with them in mind ;P<br /> <br /> Sure, being taken from your life like that sounds quite traumatic, too. Maybe Ketchup turned out the way he did b/c of all the compound stress? And he's still relatively well-adjusted, I mean, he just plotted the wholesale slaughter of a few hundreds Celestials after all...</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, there's rest. They're allowed some yearly sabbaticals, according to the manual. Though given that I'm not sure Creation has the concept of &quot;weekends&quot;, it might still come out as less free time than most of us have in our much less stressful, everything-I-know-hangs-on-the-balance jobs, and we already see a lot of burnouts and breakdowns, so I kind of tend to wonder if it's anywhere near enough. But then, this is the same edition of the game that assumed it was ridiculous and unnatural that someone with the power of a Solar exalt would be willingly subordinate to a mortal, so psychology clearly was not a huge thing here.<br /> <br /> But yeah, most of my STs have indeed played it like burnout is absolutely a risk for Sidereals, and various stripes of moderate hedonism off the clock, from drugs to brotheling to Xtreme Philosophy to just paying the equivalent of five hundred thousand bucks to get a twelve hour session from the God of Awesome Massages, are quite common among Sidereals in most tables I've been, to take the edge off things a bit. Or gardening. My third Sidereal's sifu had a massive zen garden in his manse, and a first age system keyed to it that was programmed to bodily throw out anyone who wanted to come bother him in there for anything less severe than &quot;Gem is on fire&quot; :P.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1793,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1793-drascin","user":"Drascin","date":". 08-12-2017, 05:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1793-drascin","name":"Drascin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1793_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"400"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-12T02:29:52-07:00","id":1127986,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Drascin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/1126479-sidereal-exalted-and-arcane-fate?p=1127980#post1127980\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, there's rest. They're allowed some yearly sabbaticals, according to the manual. Though given that I'm not sure Creation has the concept of &quot;weekends&quot;, it might still come out as less free time than most of us have in our much less stressful, everything-I-know-hangs-on-the-balance jobs, and we already see a lot of burnouts and breakdowns, so I kind of tend to wonder if it's anywhere near enough. But then, this is the same edition of the game that assumed it was ridiculous and unnatural that someone with the power of a Solar exalt would be willingly subordinate to a mortal, so psychology clearly was not a huge thing here.<br /> <br /> But yeah, most of my STs have indeed played it like burnout is absolutely a risk for Sidereals, and various stripes of moderate hedonism off the clock, from drugs to brotheling to Xtreme Philosophy to just paying the equivalent of five hundred thousand bucks to get a twelve hour session from the God of Awesome Massages, are quite common among Sidereals in most tables I've been, to take the edge off things a bit. Or gardening. My third Sidereal's sifu had a massive zen garden in his manse, and a first age system keyed to it that was programmed to bodily throw out anyone who wanted to come bother him in there for anything less severe than &quot;Gem is on fire&quot; :P.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;XXXtreme Philosophy!!!11&quot; sounds like fun. I imagine it plays out as a mix of pro wrestling and high speed debate, all at the same time.<br /> <br /> Yay, massages! Actually, there simply <i>must</i> be spas in Yu-Shan. Imagine how relaxing it would be... I'm starting to downright envy Sids.<br /> <br /> <i>Of course</i> Gem is on fire. When it's not exploding.<br /> <br /> (On a more serious note, the devs said in this edition Gem will no longer be 5 minutes from being destroyed in multiple apocalypses all the time. One can dream).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13651-roswynn","name":"Roswynn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13651_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"173"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-12T03:06:27-07:00","id":1127994,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Roswynn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/1126479-sidereal-exalted-and-arcane-fate?p=1127986#post1127986\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> (On a more serious note, the devs said in this edition Gem will no longer be 5 minutes from being destroyed in multiple apocalypses all the time. One can dream).</div> </div> </div> </div>Because it has already been destroyed. The Gem in the corebook is Gem That Was, a Fate Aberration which shouldn\u00b4t exist, the reflection of a city which has clearly been destroyed, and shouldn\u00b4t exist, but still does<br /> <br /> :P<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13031-clophiroth","name":"Clophiroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13031_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-12T03:47:26-07:00","id":1127997,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/1126479-sidereal-exalted-and-arcane-fate?p=1127778#post1127778\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bOr with parents; assuming that the Sidereal is somebody who, having been given access to the whole of the world still wishes to periodically visit their parents (while likely drawing from cultural inputs that don't really have things like telecommunications to condition the idea that maintaining a lifelong relationship with them when you don't live within walking distance is the norm), there are means and a bit of magic to allow that, and even then it's only a concern for a very small part of the Exalt's life. In most cases though, I would say that it's not too much different from, say, being an early European colonist to the Americas (or from one end of America to the other, during western expansion) of modest means, in which the departure means that neither shall see or communicate with one another for the rest of their lives. The difference of actually forgetting that you existed might be a bit distressing, but if you were never going to see them again anyway, the practical difference to your life is kind of minimal.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmmm, I don't think I quite agree. I mean, yes, if you're working far away, it may not make much practical difference if your parents don't remember you, but I think it makes a big emotional difference. It'd be pretty distressing.<br /> <br /> I think there's a lot of difference of course, depending on when the Sidereal was found. The Sidereals prefer to find new Sidereals as babies, and spirit them away to Yu-Shan. So for most Sidereals, it won't really be such a big deal: they'll grow up in Yu-Shan anway, raised with other young pre-Sidereals, by some nanny-gods (which also has the effect of reinforcing group loyalty).<br /> <br /> But for others, they'll grow up in their village, with their family, perhaps even get engaged or married... and then suddenly, one day, they exalt, and their own family and friends start to forget them. That's very distressing.<br /> And Sidereals growing up with their families is supposed to be more common now in the Time of Tumult (though I don't think that quite makes sense, since it's only lasted a few years, so all the Sidereals who haven't been found are presumably babies anyway).<br /> <br /> <br /> And I think it has a significant impact on the Sidereals, as it creates a distance between them and the world: their close friends are, by necessity, other Sidereals and gods. Yes, with effort, they can cultivate small relationships with normal humans, but it's very difficult for them to create anything deep*. So this has the effect of institutionalising them (plus, of course, the fact that they live in Yu-Shan anyway, that only other Sidereals really understand them, that it's a hassle to go to Creation for an evening anyway, that Yu-Shan is generally nicer than Creation, etc, etc), distancing them from the lives of ordinary people. Which makes it easier to see people as just their job, ensuring fate applies, making hard decisions.<br /> Which seems appropriate for Sidereals, genre-wise.<br /> <br /> *I suspect some Sidereals create an Arcane Destiny of a pretty normal person, and use this to make relationships with ordinary humans, but those don't last years.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 08-12-2017, 06:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-12T06:54:34-07:00","id":1128034,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/1126479-sidereal-exalted-and-arcane-fate?p=1127997#post1127997\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But for others, they'll grow up in their village, with their family, perhaps even get engaged or married... and then suddenly, one day, they exalt, and their own family and friends start to forget them. That's very distressing.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bArcane Fate is not like being friends with Dory. You have to be absent for a decent amount of time before you're actually forgotten.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">And Sidereals growing up with their families is supposed to be more common now in the Time of Tumult (though I don't think that quite makes sense, since it's only lasted a few years, so all the Sidereals who haven't been found are presumably babies anyway).</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bGiven the book that was in, I think we can write that off.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">their close friends are, by necessity, other Sidereals and gods. Yes, with effort, they can cultivate small relationships with normal humans, but it's very difficult for them to create anything deep</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bwow it sure would suck to have difficulty forming a deep long term relationship with somebody i have no idea what that would be like its probably not a thing that anybody sees as worth the effort<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-12T07:59:52-07:00","id":1128046,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/1126479-sidereal-exalted-and-arcane-fate?p=1127997#post1127997\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think there's a lot of difference of course, depending on when the Sidereal was found. The Sidereals prefer to find new Sidereals as babies, and spirit them away to Yu-Shan. So for most Sidereals, it won't really be such a big deal: they'll grow up in Yu-Shan anway, raised with other young pre-Sidereals, by some nanny-gods (which also has the effect of reinforcing group loyalty).</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly this probably needs to die in a ditch.<br /> If we got detail on a par with the Realm's schools for what that upbringing was like it could work but as it stands it's like saying Sidereals get raised in the white room because it's simulationism at the expense of characterisation.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-12T11:07:55-07:00","id":1128093,"title":"","content":"I tend to figure that Sids grow up with their original families and so on, just with a Merlin figure floating around, teaching Valuable Life Lessons and providing mentorship and so on. Whether this is a senior Sid on medical leave or a god or dragonblooded agent, they're there to teach skills and moral lessons, and make sure nothing too bad happens to the kid.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I\u00e4! I\u00e4! Moe fthagn!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/280-valles","name":"Valles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar280_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"677"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-16T04:16:00-07:00","id":1129739,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZX_XZ</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/1126479-sidereal-exalted-and-arcane-fate?p=1126615#post1126615\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> you're also going to be away training to become a Vizier for upwards of 20 years</div> </div> </div> </div>Where's that from? 20 years training seems like a huge obstacle to character concepts and/or PC advancement.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>success is the ability to go from one failure to the next without any loss of enthusiasm","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1115-the-hug-ninja","name":"The Hug Ninja","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1115_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"324"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-16T04:29:22-07:00","id":1129742,"title":"","content":"Just to provide some elaboration:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/1126479-sidereal-exalted-and-arcane-fate?p=1127997#post1127997\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Sidereals prefer to find new Sidereals as babies, and spirit them away to Yu-Shan. So for most Sidereals, it won't really be such a big deal: they'll grow up in Yu-Shan anway, raised with other young pre-Sidereals, by some nanny-gods (which also has the effect of reinforcing group loyalty).</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bThat was in Second Edition. In First Edition, the Sidereals only kept a distant watch, trying to shape the circumstances around the child to ensure that they would be prepared for the moment when their Essence would awaken, and intervening only in cases where the prospective Sidereal was abandoned or threatened with murder, not uncommon reactions to them owing to their uncanny fated nature. Even then, Sidereals only relocated the children to other, better suited families, since they lacked the time to raise children themselves (and it was probably not considered conductive to their development).<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-16T04:54:29-07:00","id":1129750,"title":"","content":"Oh, that's fine. Seems more sensible.<br /> I wasn't really arguing that this is how it was so it's how it should be: just that, how it was, is the main frame of reference for how it is.<br /> <br /> It's a bit awkward talking about the finer details of Sidereals (or Infernals, or Getimians, etc), when we don't really know how it'll work in 3rd ed.<br /> <br /> Perhaps we ought instead to talk about how we think it should work, or how we'd like it to work?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-18T04:54:49-07:00","id":1130775,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/1126479-sidereal-exalted-and-arcane-fate?p=1127997#post1127997\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And Sidereals growing up with their families is supposed to be more common now in the Time of Tumult (though I don't think that quite makes sense, since it's only lasted a few years, so all the Sidereals who haven't been found are presumably babies anyway).</div> </div> </div> </div>No, it was the <i>entire</i> Second Age, not just the ToT; though it was set up to get worse. That more and more Sidereal exalted started <i>dying</i> before their used-by-date\u200b, was one of the consequences of <i>the Usurpation</i>. <br /> <br /> Suddenly the Viziers had to face off against rogue demons, encroaching fair folk, servants of <i>the Deathlords</i>, and of course the <i>many raging Lunars</i> and even the handful of Solars. <br /> <br /> \u200bGood work, Bronze Faction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","name":"Greyman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-18T05:53:55-07:00","id":1130784,"title":"","content":"There was a dev comment a while back that the Sidereal treatment this edition would focus more on the personal and interpersonal consequences of Arcane Fate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Glorious Solar Kitten","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3907-aretii","name":"Aretii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3907_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"344"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-18T08:07:23-07:00","id":1130822,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Greyman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/1126479-sidereal-exalted-and-arcane-fate?p=1130775#post1130775\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, it was the <i>entire</i> Second Age, not just the ToT; though it was set up to get worse. That more and more Sidereal exalted started <i>dying</i> before their used-by-date\u200b, was one of the consequences of <i>the Usurpation</i>.<br /> <br /> Suddenly the Viziers had to face off against rogue demons, encroaching fair folk, servants of <i>the Deathlords</i>, and of course the <i>many raging Lunars</i> and even the handful of Solars.<br /> <br /> \u200bGood work, Bronze Faction.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, that makes a bit more sense.<br /> <br /> But yeah, you're right, it is pretty noble of them to sacrifice their own safety and even lives to save Creation from utter annihlation. They may not be the heroes Creation deserves, but they are the heroes it needs. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-19T16:34:03-07:00","id":1131503,"title":"","content":"Arcane Fate is a scary thing, but considering what Sidereals can do and have done, it is not necessarily a bad thing. Sidereals are not very well liked by Solar or Lunar Exalted. So sometimes not being easily to find is a good thing. Also, don't forget that the Pattern Spiders themselves can do horrible things to Sidereals who add too much work to their queue. Paradox can be equally frightening when it comes to astrology, and can be quite lethal to a Sidereal if the spiders are tired of being overburdened. Fading from the memory of mortals is something most Sidereals don't care about, their work in Heaven is more important than being remembered by mortals who see them rarely. <br /> <br /> Your storyteller can also rule that other sidereals and exalts remember the sidereal unless they are wearing a different resplendent destiny as well. Resplendent destinies are the disguise kit of the Sidereals. They often don't care if their disguise form is forgotten. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6162-raven79","name":"Raven79","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6162_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-20T10:00:53-07:00","id":1131763,"title":"","content":"Oh sure, it's very useful for Sidereals' jobs, but that doesn't mean that it's pleasant for Sidereals' social lives.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}